{"tool_name":"lra","contents":["bioconda","biocontainers","biotools","oeb"],"identifiers":["biotools:lra","bioconda:lra"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"lra","identifiers":["doi:10.1101/2020.11.15.383273"],"license":"USC-RL v1.0","summary":"Long read aligner for sequences and contigs","home_url":"https://github.com/ChaissonLab/LRA","keywords":["Clustering","Sequence Alignment"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":893},"biotools":{"id":"lra","home":"https://anaconda.org/bioconda/lra","summary":"the Long Read Aligner for Sequences and Contigs.\n\nLRA, the long read aligner for sequences and assembly contigs LRA is a sequence alignment program that aligns long reads from single-molecule sequencing (SMS) instruments, or megabase-scale contigs from SMS assemblies. LRA implements seed chaining sparse dynamic programming with a convex gap function to read and assembly alignment, which is also extended to allow for inversion cases. Through the Truvari analysis of LRA, Minimap2 and NGM-LR alignments. LRA achieves higher f1 score over HG002 HiFi, CLR and ONT datasets.\n\nHome: https://github.com/ChaissonLab/LRA.\n\nLong read aligner for sequences and contigs.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T11:45:50Z","last_update_date":"2026-11-12T14:24:22.666961Z","tool_type":["Library"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:lra","credit":[{"email":"mchaisso@usc.edu","name":"Mark JP Chaisson","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Genome indexing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3211"},{"term":"Read mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3198"},{"term":"Sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0292"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"},{"term":"Variant calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227"}]}],"name":"lra","owner":"Niclaskn","publication":[{"doi":"10.1101/2020.11.15.383273","type":["Preprint"]},{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pcbi.1009078","type"